    "text_delta": "R environments:\n* **HR sign-off:** Search committees are often barred from sending individual feedback until HR has fully closed the recruitment file, finalized the contract with the chosen candidate, and approved the feedback notes.\n* **Standard bureaucratic lag:** Academic committees often take 3–6 weeks to coordinate and issue formal written feedback.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\n\n1. **Send a polite, professional follow-up:**  \n   If you contacted the panel chair directly, wait another week (three weeks total), then send a brief, courteous follow-up to the HR contact or search chair reiterating that you are seeking constructive feedback to aid your future applications.\n2. **Focus inquiries entirely on professional development:**  \n   Frame your request around how you can strengthen future applications (e.g., *\"Are there specific areas in my teaching demonstration or interview presentation where I could improve?\"*). \n3. **Keep the focus forward:**  \n   Reaching the final shortlist of three for a public university lecturer position demonstrates that your profile is highly competitive. Variations in departmental \"fit\" and niche curriculum needs are often the deciding factors at the final hurdle.\n",
